== P4. Tail first: build the last 56 cells from the full pool, then fill the 200-cell head exactly ==
   tail cells: {'c': 2, 'e': 19, 'i': 35} ; joints closed while filling it in row scan: 87 interior + 22 ring, of which 15 + 2 go to the head
   K=10: free tails with at most K breaks inside: 10^54.2 ; boards the list reaches (17 + 5 colours): 10^26.69 ; exact heads per tail: 10^-27.5
   K=9: free tails with at most K breaks inside: 10^52.2 ; boards the list reaches (17 + 5 colours): 10^24.32 ; exact heads per tail: 10^-27.9
   so a tail-first search must pay a 200-cell exact search per tail and succeeds once in that many tails.
   (the review of the price memo puts an exact half-board with its own pool at 10^9 to 10^10 nodes)

